# XSH tcgetattr()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# tcgetattr() needs a terminal. The tests that need one use a pseudo-terminal (XSI), as
# does the background-group test; the descriptor-error tests need none.
# The returned baud rates are not tested: whether a terminal supports split rates is
# not discoverable and a pseudo-terminal need not keep a rate.

assertion  XSH.tcgetattr.001
anchor     functions/tcgetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/tcgetattr.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       Two tcgetattr() calls on a pseudo-terminal subsidiary, with data
           transfer, a flush and the opening and closing of another descriptor in
           between (no tcsetattr()), return 0 and the same attribute values.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
test       t/001-unchanged.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetattr.002
anchor     functions/tcgetattr.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      1988
says       tcgetattr(-1) and tcgetattr() of a closed descriptor return -1 with
           EBADF.
test       t/002-ebadf.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetattr.003
anchor     functions/tcgetattr.html#ERRORS/ENOTTY
class      required
since      1988
says       tcgetattr() of descriptors for a regular file, both ends of a pipe and
           /dev/null returns -1 with ENOTTY.
test       t/003-enotty-file.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetattr.004
anchor     functions/tcgetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       tcgetattr() is allowed from any process: a process in a background
           process group (SIGTTOU neither blocked nor ignored) gets 0 on its
           controlling terminal and is not stopped.
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
timeout    40
test       t/004-bg-allowed.c

assertion  XSH.tcgetattr.005
anchor     functions/tcgetattr.html#RATIONALE
anchor     functions/tcsetattr.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       BASE|XSI
since      1988
says       After tcsetattr() on one descriptor of a pseudo-terminal subsidiary,
           tcgetattr() on a second descriptor of it returns the same attribute
           values and shows the change (ECHO toggled).
note       XSI only for the pseudo-terminal set-up (posix_openpt() and its
           companions are XSI); the requirement itself is Base. A set-up that is
           not available is UNRESOLVED, or NOTINUSE when the facility is absent.
           The change is read back only for the ECHO flag, which every terminal
           supports.
test       t/005-second-open.c
